1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
This chapter compares two common payoff methods. The yellow cells ship with sample rows. Replace them with yours.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:12,000
The Debt Payoff tab compares two common methods using your own debts.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,500
List each debt with its balance, interest rate (APR) and minimum payment.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Type the total you can pay toward debt each month. Check says OK when it covers the minimums.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:38,500
Snowball clears a debt sooner. Avalanche usually means less interest overall.

6
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:47,000
Results show months to pay off and total interest for each method, side by side.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,500
In this sample, avalanche shows less interest, and snowball pays off the medical bill much sooner.

8
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:05,000
Pick the method you will stick with. It is a planning estimate; real lenders may compute interest daily or charge fees.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,500
Then put every minimum on Bills, plus the extra payment for your target debt, so your plan counts it.

10
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:17,500
